    "materialScheme": {
      "$description": "How the token set maps onto the M3 ColorScheme passed to MaterialTheme (Android) and used by shared Compose. Primary is intentionally NEUTRAL so switches/focus/progress stay calm; game colours live in SpyColors (CompositionLocal).",
      "dark": {
        "primary": "#F3EDE2",
        "onPrimary": "#121110",
        "tertiary": "#FF8B68",
        "surface": "#121110",
        "background": "#121110",
        "surfaceContainer": "#1C1A18",
        "surfaceContainerHigh": "#262320",
        "onSurface": "#F3EDE2",
        "onSurfaceVariant": "#A39C94",
        "outline": "#34302C",
        "error": "#FF6B78"
      },
      "light": {
        "primary": "#1A1714",
        "onPrimary": "#F3EDE2",
        "tertiary": "#AE3203",
        "surface": "#F6F2EA",
        "background": "#F6F2EA",
        "surfaceContainer": "#FFFFFF",
        "surfaceContainerHigh": "#EEE8DE",
        "onSurface": "#1A1714",
        "onSurfaceVariant": "#6B645C",
        "outline": "#DDD5C8",
        "error": "#C42B3A"
      },
      "note": "tertiary = spy tonal T70 (dark) / T40 (light). The semantic `spy` token (#FF6B3D / #C2410C) is what game UI uses; tertiary only matters for stray M3 components."
    },
